te"] [:td {} "13 – 14 October 1968"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/479"} "Estadio Olímpico Universitario, Ciudad de México"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/60746"} "19 from 14 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "By 1968 the mantle of best shot putter in the world had fallen to the shoulders of the 1964 silver medalist, " [:a {:href "/athletes/78743"} "Randy Matson"] ". Matson had set five world records since 1965. The most important came on 8 May 1965 in the Southwest Conference Meet, when he threw 20.95 (68-8¾) and followed that with 21.52. The second record was 70-7¼, the first throw ever over 70 feet. But in April 1967 he improved that by nearly a full foot, throwing 21.78 (71-5½). Matson opened with 20.54 (67-4¾) in Mexico and that settled the gold medal – it would be his best put of the competition. In fact all the top four had their best throws in round one – " [:a {:href "/athletes/79214"} "George Woods"] " (USA) with 20.12 (66-0¼), " [:a {:href "/athletes/77451"} "Eduard Gushchin"] " (URS) with 20.09 (65-11), and " [:a {:href "/athletes/69803"} "Dieter Hoffmann"] " (GDR) with 20.00 (65-7½)."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Qualifying"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "287"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/78743"} "Randy Matson"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "20.68 (1)"] [:td {} "20.54 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "317"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/79214"} "George Woods"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/coun